 n\n線上連結: https://stanford.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_9eKbmOgoRaa7
 wpcp8_iJ_g\n\nLunch Club provides affiliates of the Stanford Archaeology C
 enter with a community-oriented forum for engagement with current issues i
 n archaeology. On Nov 11\, 2026\, we will host Dr.Paul Goldstein from Univ
 ersity of California\, San Diego.\n\nAbstract:\n\nResearch on Tiwanaku cer
 amic iconography\, including eclipse imagery and a little-known system of 
 post-firing engravings\, brought me to Tiahuanacu in 2026. Though long rum
 ored to overlie an extension of the Tiwanaku UNESCO World Heritage site\, 
 the town was never systematically investigated until a 2024-25 salvage pro
 ject for a new municipal sewer system. Directed by Tiahuanacu archaeologis
 ts\, the project yielded significant finds that substantially add to and c
 omplement the Tiwanaku site museum’s collections. With funding from U.S.
  Ambassadors Fund for Cultural Preservation (AFCP)\, our project “Shared
  Heritage at Tiwanaku”\, directed by Deborah Blom\, Luis Callisaya and H
 ugo Avalos\,  will work with Tiahuanacu archaeologists\, excavation “mae
 stros”\, educators\, tour guides\, and local authorities to study the ne
 w finds and build inclusive educational materials and a new Municipal Gall
 ery exhibit.
